# ==============================================================================
# WSU Workshop: .gitignore Configuration
# ==============================================================================
# CONCEPT: Git Untracked & Ignored Files
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A .gitignore file tells Git which files and directories to intentionally omit
# from version control tracking.
#
# LECTURE TALKING POINTS:
# 1. Why ignore node_modules/?
#    - Dependencies can be gigabytes in size and contain platform-specific binaries.
#    - Anyone can recreate them deterministically using `package.json` and `npm ci`.
# 2. Why ignore .env and local secret files?
#    - Committing API keys, tokens, or passwords to Git is a critical security vulnerability.
#    - Once pushed to a remote repository (like GitHub), commit history preserves secrets forever.
# 3. Why ignore OS-specific metadata (.DS_Store, Thumbs.db)?
#    - They are auto-generated by operating system file explorers (macOS Finder / Windows Explorer).
#    - Committing them creates noisy, meaningless merge conflicts across different team members.
# 4. Pattern Syntax:
#    - Trailing slash (e.g. `dist/`): Matches directories only.
#    - Asterisk (e.g. `*.log`): Wildcard matching any file ending with that extension.
# ==============================================================================

# 1. Dependencies (re-installed via package managers)
node_modules/

# 2. Production & Build Outputs (re-generated by build scripts/tests)
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# 3. Local Environment Variables & Secrets (NEVER commit credentials!)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# 4. macOS System Files (auto-created by macOS Finder / Spotlight indexing)
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# 5. Windows System Files (auto-created by Windows Explorer image thumbnail cache)
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# 6. Logs & Diagnostic Artifacts (temporary runtime execution and error dumps)
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
